# name|primary checkout|its absolute git dir. Read by ocbi-mcp.sh for projects already in
# projects.conf: the primary checkout links $OCBI_HOME/<name>/profiles/main.json (background
# indexing as in the base config), every other worktree profiles/worktree.json (watchFiles and
# autoIndexOnStartup false; the current package ignores autoIndexOnStartup). A normal clone's primary is the checkout git itself
# confirms, so its git dir field may be left out. A bare clone has no such checkout, so its line
# pins the primary's git dir (<bare clone>/worktrees/<id>); the checkout's path, common dir and
# git dir must all match the pin, or every worktree gets profiles/worktree.json. Changing the pin
# to another checkout is an explicit reassignment of the primary: edit all three fields
# deliberately, never just the path.
#
# myproject|/home/me/src/myproject
# mybare|/home/me/src/mybare.git/main|/home/me/src/mybare.git/worktrees/main
